Service Account Compliance Communication Automation Solution 

Purpose: Define the proposed Microsoft 365 solution for notifying service account owners, collecting standardized remediation responses, tracking three communication notices per account, and producing auditable status evidence. 

Recommendation: Use one SharePoint master list record per service account, a Power Apps customized form as the response overlay, and scheduled Power Automate flows for initial notice, reminders, escalation, and status updates. Treat the submitted form and recorded send timestamps as the authoritative evidence. Read receipts may be requested as supplemental evidence, but they are not reliable proof of acknowledgment. 

Solution Summary 

The solution creates a single operational record for every noncompliant service account. Each email contains a secure link that opens the corresponding account record in a guided Power Apps form. The owner confirms ownership, acknowledges the deficiency, provides the remediation plan and date, and records any exception or dependency. Power Automate writes each successful communication back to the same account record, including separate checkboxes and timestamps for Notice 1, Notice 2, and Notice 3. 

A daily scheduled flow evaluates unresolved records against stored due dates and sends only the next eligible notice. This avoids duplicate messages, preserves the exact history by account, and provides leadership reporting without reconciling email logs manually. 

Expected Outcomes 

One authoritative record per service account from identification through remediation or enforcement. 

Standardized owner responses with conditional questions and required evidence. 

Automated initial notice, reminder, escalation, and enforcement warning based on configurable dates. 

Notice 1, Notice 2, and Notice 3 sent checkboxes with corresponding timestamps, recipients, and flow run references. 

Dashboard ready data for response rates, aging, exceptions, pending remediation, and escalation status. 

 

