Key Design Decisions 

Use one item per service account, not one item per owner. One owner may receive a consolidated email, but the flow must update each included account separately. 

Generate a deep link that opens the selected SharePoint item in the customized Power Apps form. The link must include only the item identifier and site context, not sensitive account metadata. 

Store each due date in SharePoint. Do not calculate production escalation dates from fixed dates embedded in flow actions. 

Update a notice checkbox only after the email action succeeds. A failed send remains eligible for controlled retry. 

Stop all reminder paths after a valid response, approved exception, remediation completion, or administrative hold. 

SharePoint List Design 

Recommended list name: Service Account Compliance Tracker. Enable version history. Limit editing so owners can update only the response fields through the form, while IAM administrators manage source data, deficiencies, and enforcement status. 

