Submission Behavior 

Validate required and conditional fields before Submit is enabled. 

On submit, stamp Acknowledged On and Response Submitted On and change status to Responded or Exception Pending. 

Notify IAM when assistance is requested, ownership is disputed, the account is no longer required, or the target date requires exception review. 

Display a confirmation screen containing the account name, submitted date, recorded target date, and case status. 

Prevent owners from changing notice history, deficiencies, policy references, enforcement fields, or administrative status. 

Power Automate Workflow Specification 

Flow 1  Send Initial Notice 

Trigger: Scheduled flow or approved manual batch trigger. 

Selection: Case Status = Ready to Notify; Notice 1 Sent = No; Automation Hold = No; Owner email is populated. 

Get eligible SharePoint items using an indexed OData filter. Enable pagination and define an operational batch limit. 

For each account, construct the record specific Power Apps form URL and HTML email body. 

Send from the approved shared mailbox to the account owner. Include service account metadata, detected deficiencies, policy reference, required actions, response due date, and form link. 

After a successful email action, update Notice 1 Sent = Yes, Notice 1 Sent On = current UTC time, Notice 1 Recipients, Notice 1 Flow Run ID, Case Status = Notice 1 Sent, and Receipt Status. 

On failure, write Last Automation Error and Error On. Do not select Notice 1 Sent. Notify the support queue after the configured retry threshold. 

Flow 2  Daily Reminder and Escalation 

Trigger: Recurrence once per business day after the source data refresh window. 

Get open items where Automation Hold = No and Case Status is not Remediated, Closed, or Exception Approved. 

If no valid response exists and the escalation due date is reached and Notice 2 Sent = No, send Notice 2 to the owner and configured SLT recipient. 

If the item remains unresolved and the enforcement notice date is reached and Notice 3 Sent = No, send Notice 3 to the owner, manager, SLT recipient, and enforcement review queue. 

Update only the notice fields associated with the email that succeeded. Preserve the earlier notice values. 

If a response arrives before a send action executes, recheck current item status immediately before sending to prevent a stale reminder. 

Flow 3  Process Owner Response 

Trigger: When a SharePoint item is modified, with trigger conditions that detect response field changes and prevent self triggered loops. 

Validate that required answers are present and the acknowledged checkbox is selected. 

Stamp response dates and derive the next status: Responded, In Remediation, Exception Pending, Ownership Review, or Closure Review. 

Notify IAM for assistance requests, ownership disputes, accounts marked no longer required, late target dates, interactive logon with missing CRE, or CyberArk data gaps. 

Record the notification result and do not overwrite owner supplied response values. 

Flow 4  Receipt Intake  Optional 

If the program requires read receipt collection, use an approved method that can request a receipt and a dedicated mailbox process that attempts to match incoming receipts to the account and notice number. Store unmatched receipts in an exception queue for review. This flow is supplemental and must not control escalation or closure. 

 

Read Receipt and Delivery Evidence 

Read receipts are not dependable compliance evidence. A recipient or tenant policy may decline, suppress, or prevent them. The standard Outlook Send an email V2 action records a successful connector action and places mail in Sent Items, but Microsoft documents that this action does not return a message ID. That limits deterministic receipt correlation. 

Option 

Method 

Evidence Stored 

Constraint 

Recommended baseline 

Outlook Send an email from a shared mailbox V2 

Record Notice Sent, Sent On, recipients, flow run ID, and form submission. Set Receipt Status to Not Supported or Unknown. 

Simple, supportable, auditable at the process level. Does not prove the message was opened. 

Enhanced best effort 

Microsoft Graph sendMail through an approved connection or custom connector 

Request a read receipt on the message and store a generated correlation token in the subject or body. Monitor the mailbox for returned receipts. 

May require premium licensing, security review, application permissions, and custom receipt parsing. Receipt can still be declined or suppressed. 

Authoritative acknowledgment 

Power Apps form submission 

Stamp acknowledgment and response dates on the account item. 

Use this as evidence that the owner acknowledged the issue and supplied a plan. 

 

Recommended Control Position 

Request read receipts only if stakeholders still want the signal, but do not delay escalation waiting for a receipt. Use successful send timestamps as communication evidence and the owner form submission as acknowledgment evidence. If proof of delivery is mandatory, confirm whether Exchange message trace data is available to the authorized operations team and define its retention and access requirements separately. 

Email Content Requirements 

Service account name, domain or directory, application and environment when known. 

Detected compliance deficiencies and applicable policy reference. 

Required actions and response due date. 

Secure form link for the specific account record. 

Escalation or enforcement consequence appropriate to the notice number. 

IAM contact or monitored support mailbox. 

Correlation token containing the account record ID and notice number, without sensitive data. 

 

Business Rules and Safeguards 

Rule 

Implementation 

Duplicate prevention 

A notice is eligible only when its Sent checkbox is No. Recheck the current item immediately before send. 

Successful send 

Set Sent = Yes only after the email action reports success. Stamp UTC time and recipients in the same success scope. 

Response suppression 

Do not send reminders after a valid response, approved exception, remediation, closure, or administrative hold. 

Owner change 

If ownership changes, preserve prior recipient history and direct the next notice to the current verified owner. 

Business days 

Use a maintained business calendar list or precomputed milestone dates. Do not assume addDays equals business days. 

Bulk owners 

A consolidated owner email may list multiple accounts, but every account retains its own link, notice checkbox, timestamp, and status. 

Enforcement 

Automation may notify and create a review item. Disablement or deletion requires an approved human decision and execution evidence. 

Data protection 

Do not place passwords, secrets, privileged credentials, or sensitive technical details in email or form URLs. 

Concurrency 

Use controlled concurrency or item locking when batch size is high to avoid two runs updating the same record. 

Error handling 

Use Try, Catch, and Finally scopes; capture flow run ID, failed action, error text, and retry count. 

 

Security and Access 

IAM administrators: full control of account source, deficiency, notice, status, and enforcement fields. 

Account owners: read the assigned record and edit only response fields through Power Apps. 

Leadership and auditors: read only access to reporting views or approved extracts. 

Flow service identity: least privilege access to the SharePoint list and Send As permission for the shared mailbox. 

Use environment variables or solution references for site URL, list name, shared mailbox, form URL, and escalation group. 

Apply retention, sensitivity, and audit requirements aligned to the organization policy. 

