Acceptance Criteria 

Every eligible service account receives Notice 1 once and the account item records the successful send. 

Each form link opens the intended account and owners cannot alter protected account or audit fields. 

All required and conditional questions behave as designed and valid submissions stamp the response status and date. 

Notice 2 and Notice 3 send only when their stored eligibility dates are reached and the account remains unresolved. 

A successful form response suppresses future automated reminders. 

Failed sends remain unsent, are retried according to policy, and appear in an operational error view. 

Notice history and prior recipients remain intact after owner or status changes. 

Disablement and deletion are not executed automatically without the approved control and authorization. 

 

